  "interpretations": [
    "Final PPO start right hip/knee/ankle have nonzero20ms joint motion during low-force near-ground samples; complete joint immobility is not a complete description of failed lift.",
    "Final PPO start residual RMS at these hip/knee/ankle joints is approximately.003-.006rad, far below the radius; this is not actual torque or proof that enlarging the residual will help.",
    "Reference-directed movement in an individual joint does not guarantee a coordinated sole-lift trajectory.",
    "Static target sole geometry and command/pose discrepancies do not isolate PD weakness, saturation, contact constraint, learned model error, reward, critic or exploration.",
    "Initial/final low-force masks can differ; conditional statistics are not paired causal effects. No training recipe or checkpoint adoption follows from this analysis."
  ],
